    <h1 class="page-title">USB-C dock only detecting one monitor: diagnose the display path.</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">One display working through a USB-C dock does not prove the dock is bad. The host's display limits, dock technology, cable, firmware, and display settings can all produce the same symptom. Diagnose those layers in order.</p>
    <p class="article-meta">By <a href="/about/">Keith Casko</a> · Updated <time datetime="2026-10-01">October 1, 2026</time> · <b>6 steps</b> · Based on manufacturer documentation, not a bench test</p>
